      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "Hard work is important, but preparing smart for an interview is also really important, reading through interview experiences and prepping accordingly is important.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "There is a high possibility that even though you are the smartest, you might not end up with a good offer, and that's alright because placement has a huge chunk of luck on your side.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Be true to yourself; copying projects or lying won't land you anywhere. Consistent knowledge building over time is essential.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Keep your mind open during interviews so you can think of new examples and answers; when the interviewer reaches your strongest point, dive deep into it.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Consistently do DSA; in the last 1‑2 months you can prepare for other stuff.",
          "category": "OA preparation",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Make your projects with a purpose, and if not, keep an answer ready that ties the project to a real‑world scenario.",
          "category": "Project preparation",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Losing hope and feeling demotivated is normal; believe in yourself, stay fit, eat well and sleep well during the preparation period.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 5
        }
