      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "If you're giving results (Eg. reduced response time by 80%) in your projects, make sure they’re real and not simulated.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Stay calm even if you miss something. Don’t panic. Just be honest and smile through it.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Stick to your answer unless you're really wrong.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Keep your answers honest but aligned with company values. Also, prepare a few things that aren’t in your resume — hobbies, side projects, values, or personal traits.",
          "category": "HR preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Be curious and genuine. If you don’t know something, say it confidently.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Clarify doubts before jumping into answers, they appreciate it.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Practice DSA, OOPs, DBMS, and be ready for project deep-dives.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Go for an internship, even if it’s unpaid, the experience really helps.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Explore different technologies in depth, not just at the surface level.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Make sure you have a strong understanding of everything on your resume every single detail.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Stay calm and positive, even if something goes wrong.",
