      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "Time management is very important in the first 2 sections. Questions are doable but the decision to attempt or skip a particular question based upon time is more important.",
          "category": "OA preparation",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Many python users faced issues in this round and this was seen in PhonePe as well, so if you’ve enough time consider shifting to cpp/java.",
          "category": "OA preparation",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Make sure you are clear with the basics of your first language and have some idea of OOP in Java too if java isn’t your first language. Also never ignore OOP in your first language.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Candidates whose first language is Java were also asked about development in Java (Springboot related) so be prepared.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Design problems are to check how you approach a problem so take your time and think in 360 degree, ask genuine questions related to company tech at the end.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Yes surprisingly most of us were never asked about DSA problems.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "For all your projects make a google doc with all the important points/features, their implementation and tech stack as it becomes really easy to revise.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Add to it what problems did you face and how did you resolve them as it is a check question if you’ve done the project yourself.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Whenever you feel confused, communicate with the interviewer, they’ll surely help you out.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Try to connect answers with company values. Read about their vision/mission, tagline, history.",
          "category": "HR preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "There might be some trick questions which play on our psychology so it is always safer to answer honestly.",
          "category": "HR preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Be friendly with the interviewer and reflect your true personality.",
          "category": "HR preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Prepare basics really well, not being able to answer them gives a bad impression.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Don’t consider DSA as the only way to conquer placements. Balance dev/DSA and start revising core subjects early.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Basic web dev projects won’t be enough; explore basics of devops or app dev.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Many companies were asking LLD/system design, so allocate time to these topics.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Give mock interviews with friends or seniors to build confidence and identify weak sections.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Never let rejections bring you down; focus on what you can control.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Get an internship even if it's unpaid!!!",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Consider learning LLD/system design early on.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        }
